  "text": "Skip to content\nCareers\nOpen roles\nPortfolios\nReferrals\nAbout\nLogin\nHire with 8x\nFind your role\nWhat is 8x?\n\n8x is a human orchestration company. Wherever there is a human in the loop, 8x supplies that person, evaluates the work and pays for it, across marketing, engineering and sales.\n\nRemote-first, built from San Francisco.\n\nHow the company is organised\n\nThe company is organised into verticals. Each one has a vertical lead whose focus is the value a single person can bring in that specific use case.\n\nEvery vertical runs on the same underlying principle. A large number of people are orchestrated and evaluated against one key metric for that vertical: virality potential in marketing, meetings booked in sales.\n\nEach new vertical inherits the architecture and the experience of the ones before it, so every one starts further along than the last.\n\nThe aim is billions of people under management on 8x platforms, and a different idea of what work is.\n\nWhat has been built\n8x Social\n\nA managed creator network. More than 250,000 creators across 50 countries make organic video for brands, with no ad spend behind it.\n\n8x Sales\n\nA remote sales floor. People learn to sell on real calls with live coaching, and are paid per booking and per qualified meeting.\n\n8x Business\n\nA B2B creator marketplace. Brands brief vetted LinkedIn creators and follow the work from impressions through to closed deals.\n\n8x Research\n\nAI-moderated user research. Hundreds of one-to-one interviews run in parallel and come back as ranked themes with the quotes behind them.\n\nThe founders\nJaka Bavdek\n\nCo-founder and CEO\n\nOriginally from Slovenia. Has lived in London, Singapore, India and Berlin, and took a master’s degree in London. Started a first company at 17; one of those early companies became a market leader in Slovenia. Founded Epistemy and e-Matura before 8x. Now based in San Francisco.\n\nJaka Bavdek’s site\nTheo Bui\n\nCo-founder and CTO\n\nFrench-American, based in San Francisco. Has built robotic arms, software and ride-sharing apps.\n\nTheo Bui’s site\n\nThe two met at Entrepreneur First, over a shared view of what building in the AI era takes: that distribution is becoming the most important thing a company has.\n\nWork here\n\nRoles at 8x and the companies we partner with.\n\nSee Open Roles\nFind a role\nand send us your work.\nFind your role\nOpen roles\nPortfolios\nReferrals\nAbout 8x\n\nRemote-first,\nbuilt from San Francisco.\n\n8x Careers\nBack to the beginning"
}